          { name: "Partisan Identity as a Primary Appeal", tag: "avoid", why: "At 43.6% college attainment and $70,069 income, Belknap-2 is an educated, prosperous constituency that evaluates on policy specificity and evidence-based governance rather than tribal partisan loyalty — messaging that relies on abstract conservative or progressive positioning, without grounding in the district's material economic concerns around housing, healthcare, and wage viability, will underperform relative to candidates who address these constituencies' actual governing priorities. In a district where renters and non-white communities represent roughly 40% of the population when combined with the demographic gap, inherited partisan assumptions are particularly unreliable." }
