          { name: "Assuming Young Adults Are Reliably Democratic Without Demonstrating Responsiveness", tag: "avoid", why: "Young adults in high-education, high-renter districts often register Democratic by default but do not assume automatic loyalty if their material concerns — housing, wages, healthcare, student debt — are not visibly prioritized in legislative action. A candidate who treats this constituency as a secure Democratic base rather than as voters who must be convinced that state government is actively addressing their economic constraints will invite a credible challenger to mobilize around those unmet concerns, regardless of registration advantage." }
