          { name: "Identity-Based or Ideological Campaign Framing", tag: "avoid", why: "A constituency with 31.7% college attainment and $84,484 income evaluates candidates on governance competence and concrete policy delivery, not on partisan identity or abstract ideological positioning; abstract messaging about progressive versus conservative values or appeals to partisan loyalty will not resonate with voters who have already shown willingness to switch their voting behavior based on material concerns. Candidates in this district win by demonstrating specific understanding of aging-homeowner economic security challenges and offering credible solutions — not by assuming partisan identity or ideological affinity will hold voters whose behavior in 2024 showed they prioritize governance effectiveness." }
