          "Lead with healthcare and fiscal security for aging homeowners: Medicare sustainability, prescription drug affordability, and property tax fairness are the material governance issues for a constituency with 52.5-year median age and substantial home equity — these are the issues most likely driving the Democratic margin and most vulnerable to effective Republican counter-messaging if that messaging is credible and specific rather than ideological.",
          "Engage the college-educated suburban constituency on governance competence, not partisan identity: The 31.7% college attainment rate signals voters who evaluate on policy substance and institutional effectiveness — abstract conservative or progressive positioning will not move them; specific answers to their economic security concerns and evidence of fiscal management capability will.",
          "Recognize this is a vulnerable hold or an opportunity to gain: At 53% Democratic in a district where the demographic profile suggests 55-60% Republican potential, both parties should treat this as a genuinely competitive seat in 2026 — either party can hold it or flip it based on whether they deliver on the governance expectations of older, affluent homeowners who are currently dissatisfied enough to have broken their historical partisan alignment."
