          "Identify and defend against the specific challenger argument on the incumbent's record: if Democratic, frame around healthcare affordability and property tax equity; if Republican, focus on constituent service delivery and fiscal discipline rather than ideological positioning that alienates college-educated moderates.",
          "Mobilization of homeowners aged 45-65 is the entire election — this is a constituency that votes reliably if motivated but has weak partisan attachment and high cross-partisan persuadability. A campaign that assumes the Republican base will turn out for a generic Republican will lose; one that builds genuine constituent relationship will hold.",
          "Do not campaign as though Cheshire County is conservative territory — it is affluent, college-educated, and fiscally moderate, which means a candidate perceived as ideologically extreme or indifferent to healthcare access will lose educated women and professionals who are the marginal voters in this 51-49 split."
