          { name: "Ceding Swing Constituencies by Default", tag: "avoid", why: "In a 50-50 district, assuming that renters will default to one party, that older homeowners will default to another, or that any demographic group is 'safe' is strategically naive. The renter-homeowner divide, the age-based economic divergence, and any communities represented by the 8.6% demographic gap are all swing terrain — candidates who engage these groups with specific policy answers will consolidate support more effectively than those who treat them as inevitable constituencies or write them off entirely." }
