          "Lead with housing affordability and wage standards: the $92,148 median income masks a 35% renter population for whom housing is the primary budget constraint, and Hispanic households in particular are concentrated in the lower-income and renter segments where rent-to-income ratios are unsustainable — this is both a governance issue and the most credible way to activate Hispanic voter participation.",
          "Address healthcare access specifically for the Hispanic community: coverage gaps, language barriers in provider networks, and rural health access in exurban Hillsborough County are concrete constituent needs that require candidates to demonstrate fluency, not generic Democratic healthcare rhetoric.",
