          "Lead with fiscal responsibility and education quality: at $109,296 median income with 41.1% college attainment, this constituency is financially literate and views education as both a public good and an economic asset — tax policy, school funding, and the state's education ranking relative to regional peers are the governance questions most likely to drive voting behavior.",
          "Address the affluent, educated centrist voter directly: this district's demographic profile produces voters who may disagree with partisan orthodoxy on environmental regulation, social issues, or the role of government in public goods — any candidate who assumes that high income automatically produces conservative voting across all issues is misreading this constituency.",
          "Build a candidate-specific case for election, not just a partisan case: the split result proves that personal credibility, professional accomplishment, and demonstrated local governance competence matter more in this district than party registration — focus on what makes you specifically qualified to represent Hillsborough-16, not on partisan identity."
