          "Engage the 39.7% renter constituency directly: With 39.7% renter rates in a $91,495 median income district, housing affordability and rental market regulation are material issues for a significant share of the electorate. Renters in affluent markets often face acute affordability pressure despite overall district wealth; a specific housing strategy is more credible than generic economic messaging.",
          "Build a ticket that reflects educational and professional diversity: In a 45.9% college-educated district with a 69% Democratic vote share, the electorate is evaluating candidate quality and expertise directly. Running candidates with demonstrable professional competence, constituent service records, or specific policy expertise in areas voters care about (education funding, local fiscal management, regional economic development) is more effective than partisan appeals alone.",
