          "Engage the Hispanic community with specificity on economic mobility, workplace protections, and family economic stability — the 15% Hispanic population in a working-class district is both a reliable Democratic base if activated around economic concerns and a swing constituency sensitive to whether government demonstrates competence on their material needs.",
          "Consolidate the homeowner and higher-income Republican minority without conceding the renter majority — the 37% Republican result indicates a real constituency of homeowners and professionals who believe Republican economic policy serves them better; winning or holding requires defending this base while also demonstrating to swing renters that your party's approach to housing and wages is credible.",
          "Recognize the 2-seat at-large structure creates genuine two-candidate competition — both seats are contested because the district is genuinely divided; any candidate who treats a 63-37 result as a safe mandate or assumes inherited party voters will automatically show up is not reading the competitive reality correctly."
