          "Build a credible education and healthcare platform for affluent suburban voters: at 58.4% college education and 51.6-year median age, this constituency has concrete stakes in higher education funding, K-12 quality, and Medicare/healthcare stability — Republicans will need to articulate specific education and healthcare policy that competes for educated, aging, affluent voters' trust.",
          "Do not cede the fiscal governance frame: although Democrats swept the seat at 79%, affluent suburban voters with $100,246 income retain skepticism about government spending and have high expectations for competent administration — a Republican candidate who emphasizes fiscal discipline, efficient governance, and strategic budget prioritization has a real opening with this constituency.",
          "Engage renters and younger professionals specifically: the 41.9% renter rate is unusually high for an affluent district and likely includes younger dual-professional households with student debt and housing cost sensitivity — Republicans should test whether messaging around housing affordability, wage growth, and inflation resonates with this segment and competes for their vote in future cycles."
