          "Build active constituent engagement infrastructure now, while unopposed: town halls focused on renter concerns, workforce development forums with college-educated professionals, and direct relationship-building with minority communities will make the seat durable when a challenger inevitably emerges. Treat unopposed victory as an urgent opportunity to build relationships, not as license to reduce engagement."
