        issues: [
          { name: "Fiscal Management and Healthcare Cost Control", tag: "lean-into", why: "At $121,875 median household income and 62% college education, Rockingham-21 is a constituency of affluent professionals and retirees who evaluate legislators on concrete fiscal performance — property tax management, education funding efficiency, and healthcare cost trajectory — rather than partisan messaging. The incumbent's legislative record on these material concerns is the primary determinant of whether the seat remains Democratic in a credible contest; this affluent, educated district will not reward incumbency without demonstrated fiscal competence." },
          { name: "Education Funding and School Quality", tag: "lean-into", why: "With 62% college-educated adults and a 47.5-year median age, this district is composed largely of parents invested in K-12 education quality and college access pathway. State education funding levels, school district resources, and the quality of public education relative to neighboring districts are the primary fiscal policy concerns for this constituency. An incumbent who articulates a specific vision for education funding and can demonstrate legislative results on school resources will consolidate support among the district's educated, affluent parents." },
          { name: "Renter Community Economic Security", tag: "careful", why: "Although homeowners comprise 57.4% of the district, the 42.6% renter rate represents a meaningful and often-invisible constituency — younger adults, service-sector workers, and professionals in transition whose economic concerns (housing costs, wage growth, opportunity mobility) differ substantially from the homeowner majority. This group is not concentrated in a specific geographic pocket of the district and can become overlooked in campaigns focused on the affluent homeowner base; however, renter turnout and preference in a low-turnout state legislative race can be decisive in a marginal contest." },
          { name: "Partisan Polarization Rhetoric", tag: "avoid", why: "This is a district of affluent, educated professionals and retirees who are skeptical of partisan extremism and vote on specific governance performance rather than tribal affiliation. An incumbent who campaigns primarily on partisan messaging or abstract ideological positioning will fail to meet the intellectual expectations of a 62% college-educated constituency that expects substantive policy discussion and fiscal accountability." },
          { name: "Taking Unopposed Status as Evidence of Structural Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "The 2024 unopposed result is a specific artifact of Republican recruitment failure and Mandelbaum's incumbency advantage in this election cycle, not evidence that Rockingham-21 is structurally Democratic. In a district with this income, education level, and homeownership rate, a credible Republican challenger will enter the next cycle in a demographically favorable position. Any incumbent strategy that treats this election's unopposed status as proof of durable Democratic hold in a swing county will be strategically surprised." }
        ],
        memoHeadline: "NH-HD-Rockingham-21: A Wealthy, Educated, Aging District with Unopposed Democratic Incumbency and Structural Vulnerability to Credible Republican Challenge",
        memoParagraphs: [
          "NH-HD-Rockingham-21 is a district of substantial affluence and educational attainment — $121,875 median household income (among the highest in New Hampshire), 62.0% college education, 87.4% white, 47.5 median age — with a demographic profile that, in most competitive American districts, would produce a Republican or highly marginal result. The unopposed 2024 Democratic victory is not a measure of partisan strength; it is a measure of opponent absence. This district's demographics — high income, high education, aging homeowner base with 57.4% ownership — create a natural Republican target when a credible candidate emerges. The 42.6% renter rate, while substantial, still means the district is homeowner-majority and asset-holding; this is not a Democratic stronghold by demographic logic, but a district where Democratic incumbency has faced no test. The intellectual and economic profile of the constituency — college-educated affluent professionals and retirees — suggests voters who evaluate on specific policy performance and candidate credibility rather than partisan default.",
          "The 2024 unopposed result should be read as a warning indicator rather than a stability signal. Rockingham County, which contains this district, is part of southeastern New Hampshire's suburban-exurban corridor and has been a competitive battleground in recent statewide elections; a district this wealthy and educated, in a county this politically volatile, should expect challenger emergence in the next cycle when the seat is no longer held by an incumbent with organizational advantage. The Democratic incumbent, Mandelbaum, benefits from an open field in 2024, but that advantage is specific to this cycle. A Republican challenger with credible standing in this affluent, educated community — someone who can speak to tax policy, education funding, healthcare costs, and fiscal management with specificity matching the constituency's intellectual demands — enters the race in a structurally favorable position. The very factors that produced the unopposed result (Mandelbaum's local standing, Democratic incumbency advantage, Republican recruitment failure) are specific to this election and will not persist automatically into the next one. Any Democratic strategist should treat Rockingham-21 as a seat requiring active defense, not a safe hold."
        ],
        memoBullets: [
          "Recognize that unopposed status in 2024 masks structural vulnerability: $121,875 income and 62% college education are not baseline Democratic strengths, and a credible Republican candidate will enter the next cycle in a demographically favorable position. Build constituent relationships and legislative record now that create durability beyond incumbent name recognition.",
          "Engage the affluent, educated constituency on fiscal management and healthcare cost control: this is not a district moved by partisan rhetoric, but by tangible governance performance on taxes, education funding quality, and whether government is delivering value. Mandelbaum should articulate a specific legislative record on these material concerns rather than relying on incumbency advantage alone.",
          "The 42.6% renter rate represents meaningful economic diversity within the district's affluence — younger adults, service-sector workers, and professionals in transition who have different economic security concerns than the homeowner majority. Active engagement with this constituency on housing costs, wage growth, and opportunity mobility will strengthen the incumbent's base beyond homeowner assumption.",
          "Monitor Rockingham County's broader political shifts closely: this is a swing county in statewide elections, and district-level vulnerability can emerge quickly when county-level movements accelerate. Mandelbaum should build a campaign infrastructure that can activate rapidly if a credible Republican challenger emerges in the next cycle."
        ]
