          { name: "Treating 57% as a Safe Consolidation in a Competitive Statewide Environment", tag: "avoid", why: "New Hampshire's state House competitive environment and the 1-percentage-point gap between Rockingham-23's presidential Democratic lean and Maggiore's actual 57% margin create a risk that the incumbent treats this seat as securely held when the numbers suggest otherwise. In a statewide political environment where suburban, college-educated, older constituencies are increasingly moveable based on governance competence and fiscal alignment rather than inherited partisan loyalty, assuming that 57% is a floor rather than a current position invites a well-executed challenger campaign to exploit the margin gap and recruit swing voters from the district's core demographic." }
