          "Engage the renter community with housing affordability specificity: at 41.6% of the district, renters represent a genuine swing constituency whose economic pressures are distinct from homeowners, and candidates who address this segment's concerns directly build persuadion opportunity that generic working-family messaging cannot reach.",
          "Understand the 45% opposition as a strategic intelligence problem: identify specifically whether opposition is concentrated among renters frustrated by affordability, persuadable homeowners with local governance grievances, or both — and offer concrete policy answers rather than partisan messaging.",
          "Do not rely on demographic homogeneity to assume partisan stability: 90% white population does not translate to automatic Republican loyalty in a district where 41.6% of households face housing cost pressure and 45% voted for the opposition; durable Republican advantage requires demonstrating that conservative governance delivers better results for working families' economic security than the alternative."
