          "Deliver specific messaging on wage growth and childcare affordability: the 42-year median age combined with renter-majority status suggests working-age adults with family obligations and childcare expenses; candidates who offer concrete policy positions on childcare subsidies, wage floors, and employer practices will resonate more effectively than abstract economic positioning.",
          "Do not assume the 52% result is durable or that the 48% opposition is inert: in a district of working-class renters without strong demographic diversity, voting behavior is driven by evaluation of economic conditions and perceived legislative delivery; any incumbent who campaigns as though 52% represents a safe hold rather than a contested plurality will be vulnerable to a credible challenger who focuses on household financial stress.",
