          "NH-SD-17 presents a deceptive electoral picture. The 58% Republican margin and affluent demographics — $97,057 median household income, 32.6% college attainment, 92.31% white, 16.1% renter rate — all suggest a stable conservative constituency. However, the 43.3-year median age and high homeownership concentration reveal a district built on asset-rich but income-constrained older adults whose financial security depends on healthcare costs, property tax management, and the stability of fixed incomes in an inflationary environment. The 42% Democratic share in a district this affluent and white is the first analytical flag: a Democratic vote share at this level in a New Hampshire state senate district suggests that opposition is not limited to young renters or struggling families, but includes affluent homeowners evaluating the incumbent on material grounds. The 58-42 margin is genuine but not durable — it reflects current alignment, not demographic destiny.",
