          "Lead with renter and housing economy specifics: at 36.3% renters and $86,998 median income, this is a district where housing affordability, rental market regulation, and property tax fairness are direct quality-of-life issues that motivate vote choice. Generic rhetoric about free markets or tax cuts will not move voters whose primary concern is whether they can afford to stay in their community.",
