          "Contest the Hispanic vote aggressively and specifically: the 12.51% Hispanic population is growing and educationally mobile, and Republicans have demonstrated capacity to make inroads with Hispanic voters on economic messaging. Engage Hispanic voters on wages, small business access to capital, and education costs—not just cultural identity—or watch the 44% opposition grow within this crucial swing community.",
          "Address the college-educated renter cohort directly: at 34.5% college-educated, this district includes young professionals with student debt, housing affordability constraints, and professional opportunity concerns that are distinct from both working-class and wealthy constituencies. Messaging that resonates with 28-year-old teachers, social workers, and engineers paying $1,800 rent is not the same as messaging that works with either demographic extreme.",
          "Treat 56% as a plurality under active contestation, not a Democratic floor: in a district where 44% voted opposition and all core demographics (renters, young adults, Hispanic voters) are politically mobile and responsive to economic outcomes, the incumbent cannot assume 2024 loyalty translates to 2026 turnout or preference. Build a campaign around sustained constituent engagement, economic delivery, and specific answers to the opposition's economic critique."
