          "Engage the college-educated professional class (38.7%) on fiscal management and return on public investment: this constituency evaluates government effectiveness on outcomes, not partisan loyalty — demonstrate that conservative governance delivers better stewardship of tax dollars than the Democratic alternative.",
          "Address healthcare access and cost directly: at 45.0 median age with significant asset wealth, healthcare affordability in retirement is both a material concern and a point of Democratic opposition penetration; a candidate who offers specific, credible solutions on healthcare costs consolidates affluent retiree support more effectively than one who dismisses the concern as 'socialism.'",
          "Do not take the 64% margin as a stable foundation: the 36% opposition in a high-income, highly educated district reflects real policy disagreements on healthcare, environment, and public investment — not apathy or lack of sophistication; treating this opposition as uninformed or marginal will create electoral vulnerability over successive cycles."
